# armour/shared/pauldron_fur4_l: the small leather shoulder pad on the left shoulder (fur.4; LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.6):
# (FORGE-MANTLE) fur.4: its base views repeat fur.2's small leather pad, so a 0-forge leather or padded look at pauldron dial 4 draws what it drew before; the fur MANTLE is the forge styles' replace views.
# the right one's cap lit from the top-left as it falls on this side; `when furtrim` a fur edge on its rim.
# Finish regions: R the rim, P the cap's face, W a spot on the shadow side. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
role pauldron fur.4
layer armNear
anchor shoulderL
keys pauld
z 5
side L
# (FORGE-MANTLE, round 2) `when shoulder-fur replace` views: the fur MANTLE drawn for the forge styles (STYLE_P2 28.3; generated by FORGE-MANTLE gen.py from shapes5.py); 0-forge looks keep the base views.

view D key rest origin 3 2
|.fff.
|fihgf
|fhggf
|.fff.
regions
|.....
|.PP..
|.RRW.
|.....


